---
alwaysApply: true
description: Quality gates, linting, testing, and performance expectations
---

## Code Quality

- Match existing formatting; do not reformat unrelated code.
- Add imports and types explicitly; avoid `any` in TypeScript.

## Linting and Tests

- No new linter errors allowed.
- Add targeted unit tests for new logic, especially ETL rules.

## Performance

- Optimize queries with proper indexes and filters.
- Avoid N+1; batch queries in services.
- Memoize expensive computations in React; virtualize large lists.

## File Size Limits

- Enforce per-file limits: backend 300 lines; frontend 200 lines.
